    "type": "Writer",
    "image": "ODuinnin.png",
    "description": "A priest, scholar, editor, lexicographer and a leading figure in the Gaelic Revival. Ó Duinnín devoted his life to preserving and promoting the Irish language. He compiled the Foclóir Gaedhilge agus Béarla (Irish-English Dictionary), first published in 1904 and expanded in 1927. For decades it was the standard dictionary of the Irish language.",
